  "method_adaptations": [
    "Independent biological unit is 11 constructs; average five models within seed and seeds within construct; retain all 56 seeds for resampling.",
    "Cluster selection and feature filtering use no activity labels; submission table is post hoc comparison only.",
    "Use raw CP probability units as primary geometry; feature-wise zscore is a separately reported sensitivity analysis.",
    "For 11 constructs restrict non-density k range to 2–4; record singleton and noise membership.",
    "Evaluate all methods in original CP geometry as well as fitted geometry; do not compare distinct embeddings only through their native silhouette.",
    "GMM uses low fixed-dimensional PCA and constrained covariance; BIC comparisons require exactly the same input representation.",
    "DBSCAN and HDBSCAN failures, single-cluster and all-noise results must remain in the result table.",
    "UMAP default n_neighbors=30 and min_cluster_size=15 are unsuitable for 11 constructs; use several small neighborhoods and random seeds and label results exploratory.",
    "Resample whole seeds within construct and refit feature selection and transformations inside each bootstrap.",
    "Do not suppress all warnings; record numerical failures and convergence warnings."
  ],
